# DRAFT for .github/CODEOWNERS. Not active: this branch may not edit .github/ (docs/7-quality.md, owner step 6).
#
# A CODEOWNERS file asks the named people or teams to review a change to these paths. It blocks a merge only when
# the branch protection rule "Require review from Code Owners" is on (settings.md). Every owner below is a
# placeholder: the owners of the repository decide who owns what, and write real @user or @org/team names.
# Until then this file is not valid CODEOWNERS.
#
# The paths are the ones where a mistake is a security or a supply-chain mistake. Later lines win in CODEOWNERS.

/back/server/       OPEN: owners
/docs/adr/          OPEN: owners
/nix/               OPEN: owners
/SECURITY.md        OPEN: owners
/.github/           OPEN: owners
